  "notes": "FV-002 (Wave 7): the web formal-pass manifest. Freezes the FV-CATALOG \u00a73 scenes as runner inputs: journey id, gateway mode=real (the --gateway command), the per-scene assertion set (the existing lab assertions), \u00d73 runs (the w6 convention). Mock-gateway captures are NOT formal evidence (addendum \u00a71) \u2014 the manifest requires the real Rust gateway. E-1 bound (named): the supervised runtime is unauthenticated in the lab; live-turn depth is bounded to honest states, exactly like Linux L-1. Path law: the gateway command is relative to the driver's spawn cwd (web/) \u2014 ../target/debug/flauz-web-gateway is the repo-root cargo target; --web-root dist is web/dist relative to the same cwd. Execution order: the scenes array is the suite's sequential execution order (the classic driver order \u2014 j-01..j-06, j-08, j-13..j-15, j-09, DOMAIN-NEUTRAL, A11Y; the journeys share one page per run, e.g. j-02 opens the Context inspector on the session j-01 created); a --scene filter runs the manifest prefix through the requested scene.",
